    "title": "Cut Watch is On at the Masters - Yahoo Sports",
    "text": "AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementTRENDINGNBA Play-In TournamentNFL mock draft 8.1LIV Golf's murky futureNBA Mock Draft 2.0MLB Power RankingsStory byCut Watch is On at the MastersRiley HamelThu, April 9, 2026 at 6:37 PM CDT·1 min readAdd Yahoo Sports on GoogleThere are plenty of big names in danger of missing the cut at the Masters after a tough opening round at Augusta National.AUGUSTA, Ga. — Augusta National is firm, fast, and fiery—and it’s only Thursday! If the Green Jackets want to see carnage over the weekend, the golf course is in the perfect spot to produce just that.AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementWith the first 18 holes of the 90th Masters now in the books, Rory McIlroy is tied for the lead at 5 under alongside Sam Burns. In all, only five players shot in the 60s, and just 15 players are under par—a proper test!According to Data Golf, the most likely cut number is 5 over. Accordingly, the top 50 players and ties will make it to the weekend. There are plenty of stars who need to battle on Friday to ensure they have a spot on the tee sheet come Saturday morning.RELATED:How to Watch the MastersBig Names in Danger of Missing the Cut at the Masters2 over: Ludvig Aberg, Matt Fitzpatrick, Collin Morikawa, J.J. Spaun, and Tyrrell HattonAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisement3 over: Viktor Hovland4 over: Bryson DeChambeau5 over: Patrick Cantlay6 over: Jon Rahm, Min Woo Lee8 over: Robert MacIntyreAdvertisementTerms and Privacy PolicyPrivacy DashboardAbout Our AdsAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisement",
